1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,867
This is the screen you'll use most:
attaching a 3D model to one of your

2
00:00:06,077 --> 00:00:08,068
Open Product 3D Models from the nav.

3
00:00:08,128 --> 00:00:12,626
Every product in your store is listed
here, newest first, and each row tells you

4
00:00:12,686 --> 00:00:14,393
whether it already has a model.

5
00:00:15,253 --> 00:00:19,126
The subtitle under the heading is your
coverage: three of twenty-four products

6
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:19,786
have a model.

7
00:00:19,842 --> 00:00:23,413
It's the single number that tells you how
much of the catalogue is done.

8
00:00:24,273 --> 00:00:26,289
With a big catalogue, search by title.

9
00:00:26,349 --> 00:00:30,659
It's server-side and debounced, so it
searches your whole store rather than just

10
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:32,133
the page you're looking at.

11
00:00:32,993 --> 00:00:36,569
A green cube and the words 3D model
assigned mean that product is live.

12
00:00:36,629 --> 00:00:39,641
The button on the right changes from Add
to Update to match.

13
00:00:40,501 --> 00:00:45,164
Click a product — anywhere on the row, or
the Add button — to open its detail

14
00:00:45,224 --> 00:00:45,824
screen.

15
00:00:46,203 --> 00:00:48,066
Here's a product with no model yet.

16
00:00:48,126 --> 00:00:51,197
On the left, the model file card and the
viewer settings.

17
00:00:51,257 --> 00:00:55,810
On the right, a live preview that's
currently empty because there's nothing to

18
00:00:56,670 --> 00:01:01,044
Read the card description, because it's
the rules. Glb or gltf only.

19
00:01:01,104 --> 00:01:02,544
Up to twenty megabytes.

20
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:07,630
Stored in your Shopify Files, and linked
to the product through the custom dot

21
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:09,586
model underscore 3D metafield.

22
00:01:10,446 --> 00:01:14,985
You have two ways to get a model in.
Upload sends a new file from your

23
00:01:15,045 --> 00:01:19,699
Choose from Files reuses something already
in your Shopify Files — useful when the

24
00:01:19,759 --> 00:01:24,183
same model belongs to several products,
because it doesn't duplicate the file.

25
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:28,437
Let's upload. Click Upload, pick your .
glb, and open it.

26
00:01:28,497 --> 00:01:33,528
The app validates the file before it sends
anything — wrong extension or over twenty

27
00:01:33,588 --> 00:01:37,770
megabytes and you get told immediately
instead of after a long upload.

28
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:43,291
The upload goes through Shopify's staged
upload, so the file lands in your Files,

29
00:01:43,351 --> 00:01:45,156
then gets linked to the product.

30
00:01:45,216 --> 00:01:46,614
Big models take a moment.

31
00:01:47,474 --> 00:01:48,074
Done.

32
00:01:47,789 --> 00:01:53,017
The file URL appears, the header now says
3D model assigned, and the live preview is

33
00:01:53,077 --> 00:01:54,780
rendering your actual model.

34
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:58,192
Once a model is assigned, two things
change.

35
00:01:58,252 --> 00:02:02,761
Upload becomes Upload Replace, which swaps
the file but keeps all your viewer

36
00:02:02,821 --> 00:02:03,421
settings.

37
00:02:03,356 --> 00:02:08,043
And Remove appears — that unlinks the
model from the product; it does not delete

38
00:02:08,103 --> 00:02:10,002
the file from your Shopify Files.

39
00:02:10,862 --> 00:02:12,901
Choose from Files opens this picker.

40
00:02:12,961 --> 00:02:17,741
It lists only model files, tells you which
one is currently assigned, and searching

41
00:02:17,801 --> 00:02:18,907
filters as you type.

42
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:23,397
Pick one and it's assigned instantly — no
second upload of the same geometry.

43
00:02:24,257 --> 00:02:26,961
One thing to know: the plan limit is
checked here.

44
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:31,438
If you're at your limit and try to assign
a model to a new product, the app stops

45
00:02:31,498 --> 00:02:32,323
you and says so.

46
00:02:32,383 --> 00:02:36,192
Replacing a model on a product that
already has one is always allowed.

47
00:02:37,052 --> 00:02:41,261
And that's it — the product page picks the
model up from the metafield with no

48
00:02:41,321 --> 00:02:41,973
further work.

49
00:02:42,033 --> 00:02:43,177
Assign, and it's live.

50
00:02:44,037 --> 00:02:44,825
Model assigned.

51
00:02:44,885 --> 00:02:49,519
Next we open up the viewer settings, which
is where this app really earns its keep.
